# Cursor token habits (#1970)

Apply in every repo and chat. Tool calls re-read the whole chat; cache reads dominate the bill.

## Habits
- One chat per ticket/task. After merge or half-context: hand off (ticket/task, PR/branch, what's left) and stop.
- Prefer `gh`/`curl`/APIs/repo scripts over browser clicking. Unavoidable clicking, wide search, or CI digs → use a subagent and keep only its summary.
- Keep tool output small: `rg`/`tail`, viewport screenshots, wait scripts — not poll loops.
- Don't re-verify what was already confirmed. Put generated media/build output in `.gitignore` (`git status` is attached every turn).

## Spend by Cursor plan %
- Under 70%: normal models for the task size.
- At/over 70%: prefer cheap models and subagents; Auto/Haiku/Composer for questions and small edits.
- At/over 100% (on demand): every token is billed — short chats, early handoffs, no expensive models unless Carlos asks.

## Task size → model
- Question: Auto or Haiku/Composer-class; no worktree/ticket unless it becomes work.
- Small edit: Auto or Composer/Sonnet-class; read only the named files.
- Medium: Sonnet-class; named/likely files before searching; explore subagent for wider search.
- Large: plan first; strong model for design; subagents for search and CI.

## Enforcement (global hooks / CursorQuota)
- Short asks `quota` / `usage` / `budget` are answered by the token-preflight hook with no model (prefix `agent:` to force the agent).
- Past ~half context (~200 KB transcript): hand off once to a new chat; do not keep burning the long thread.
- Over 70% plan + expensive model on a question/small ask: switch to a cheaper model (or resend to keep).
